hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18200","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, he said: Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Al-Awzai narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Fayruz al-Daylami, from his father, that they embraced Islam, and he was among those who embraced Islam. So they sent their delegation to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with their pledge and their Islam, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, accepted that from them. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, we are of those you have known, and we have come from where you have known, and we have embraced Islam, so who is our guardian? He said: Allah and His Messenger. They said: It suffices us, we are pleased."
"18201","Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Damrah narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Shaybani from Ibn Fayruz al-Daylami from his father, Haytham once said from Abdullah ibn Fayruz from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we are those whom you know and we have come from where you know, so who is our guardian. He said: Allah and His Messenger."
"18202","Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Damrah informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Amr from Ibn Fayruz al-Daylami from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam will surely be undone loop by loop just as a rope is undone strand by strand."
"18203","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Luhayyah narrated to us from Abu Wahb al-Jayshani from al-Dahhak ibn Fayruz that his father Fayruz embraced Islam while married to two sisters, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Divorce whichever of them you wish."
"18204","And Yahya once said: Ibn Luhayyah narrated to us from Wahb ibn Abdullah al-Maafiri from al-Dahhak ibn Fayruz from his father that he embraced Islam."
"18205","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Luhayyah narrated to us from Abu Wahb al-Jayshani from al-Dahhak ibn Fayruz from his father, he said: I embraced Islam while I had two wives who were sisters, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to divorce one of them."
"18206","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ayyash ibn Ayyash that is Ismail narrated to us, Yahya that is Ibn Abi Amr al-Shaybani narrated to me from Abdullah ibn al-Daylami from his father Fayruz, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are owners of grapes and vines and the prohibition of wine has come down, so what shall we do with them. He said: You will make them raisins. He said: What shall we do with the raisins. He said: You will soak them for your morning meal and drink them for your evening meal, and soak them for your evening meal and drink them for your morning meal. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are those whom you know and we dwell among those whom you know, so who is our guardian. He said: Allah and His Messenger. He said: I said: It suffices me, O Messenger of Allah."
